  "name": "Example: Integrating Sine and Cosine",
  "problem": "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int 3\\sin{x}\\,\\textrm d x.$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that\n\n$$\n\\int \\sin x \\, \\textrm dx = -\\cos x + C.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 3sin\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x & =3\\int sin\u2061x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(-cos\u2061x)+C \\\\  & =-3cos\u2061x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
